# Physics 12 - written explanations (round 3)
@phys12-u1-q01
W: Pressure = force ÷ area: P = F/A. | Units: N ÷ m² = N/m². | 1 N/m² is called 1 pascal (Pa) – answer B.
T: Newton = force, joule = energy, watt = power.
@phys12-u1-q02
W: Liquid pressure P = ρgh. | It depends on the depth h, the density ρ and g. | It does not depend on the shape or surface area of the container – answer C.
T: A narrow tube and a wide dam at the same depth feel the same pressure.
@phys12-u1-q03
W: A floating object is in equilibrium: upthrust = weight. | Archimedes: upthrust = weight of fluid displaced. | So a floating boat displaces its own weight of water – answer A.
T: Law of flotation: floating object displaces its own weight of fluid.
@phys12-u2-q01
W: Each photon gives its energy to one electron: K_max = hf − φ, which depends on frequency, not intensity. | Doubling the intensity doubles the number of photons arriving per second. | So twice as many electrons are emitted per second, each with the same K_max – answer D.
T: Intensity → number of electrons; frequency → their energy.
